# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later
#
# cross-check.tji - serializer cross-check report (docs/phases/phase-0.md,
# section 6.2, step 5).
#
# record-native.mjs copies this file into the plan's workspace and runs the
# real tj3 CLI from engine/tj/bin with it as a second input file, with
# cross-check-shim.rb preloaded:
#
#   tj3 --silent --no-color -f --report mainspring_crosscheck \
#       <workspace>/<entry> <workspace>/mainspring-cross-check.tji
#
# tj3 then writes mainspring-cross-check.csv (into its working directory) with
# one row per task and active scenario: scenario name, full task id, start
# and end in UTC, the task's precursors and its completion. The script checks
# them against what the shared serializer (engine/bridge/serialize.rb) wrote
# into the golden file. Parity alone cannot catch serializer bugs, because
# both sides run the same serializer.
#
# Precursors (schema v2, docs/phases/phase-2.md 5.3) is TaskJuggler's own
# list of the dependencies that end at this task: its `depends` entries and
# other tasks' `precedes` entries that name it, each printed by the listitem
# below as "<other task id> <dependency>", where the dependency is ]->[, [->[,
# ]->] or [->] (TaskScenario#query_precursors). The script derives the same
# list from the golden's depends and precedes (cross-check-rows.mjs
# expectedLinkRows), so the other task and both ends of every edge are
# checked. Completion checks a `complete` the plan sets, as tj3 prints it: the
# integer part and '%'. Precursors are compared only when the golden's result
# is ok, and for any other run the script removes the precursors line: tj3
# cannot report them for a scenario scheduling never prepared
# (cross-check-rows.mjs withoutPrecursors).
#
# TaskJuggler's task report has no column for gaps, the scheduling direction
# (`scheduling` prints ASAP for every leaf, TaskScenario.rb:1538), the
# project's working time or dailyworkinghours, so those v2 fields are covered
# by parity and the bridge fixtures only.
#
# The report's scenario list must name scenarios that exist, so the script
# rewrites the body of the macro below to the plan's active scenario ids, in
# pre-order. Left as is, the file works for plans whose top scenario is the
# default `plan`.

macro mainspring_crosscheck_scenarios [plan]

taskreport mainspring_crosscheck "mainspring-cross-check" {
  formats csv
  timezone "UTC"
  timeformat "%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ"
  scenarios ${mainspring_crosscheck_scenarios}
  columns scenario, id, start, end,
          precursors { listitem "<-query attribute='id'-> <-query attribute='dependency'->" },
          complete
  hidetask 0
  sorttasks tree, seqno.up
}
